# Cases for core-language-docs/sequences.md. Read by ../run-all.sh, which
# discovers every */CASES under snippets/ rather than carrying a list.
#
# Five pipe-separated fields:
#
#   module | cfg | expected-rc | distinct-states | what it shows
#
# A blank line or a line opening with # is skipped.
#
# THE FOURTH FIELD IS THE STATE COUNT. On this page the exit code carries most
# of the argument, since 12 of the 22 cases are evaluation failures and the
# whole point of them is that the run stops. Four counts still do real work:
#
#   Conveyor 4            the belt a zero index and a past-the-end slice run on
#   Spool 7 twice         Seq(Colors) as an invariant checks every state the
#                         bounded union checks, so the two counts must agree
#   SpoolAny 0            Init drew from Seq(Colors) and nothing was checked
#
# SpoolAny is the one to protect, for the reason the sets manifest gives about
# Caliper. A run that finds 0 distinct states has told you nothing about the
# system, and only the count says so. Leave the field empty where the page
# quotes no count.
#
# THE 75 AND 76 ROWS ARE A MATCHED PAIR, not two spellings of one thing.
# Trim/TrimPastEnd and Conveyor/ConveyorSlice are the same out-of-domain
# SubSeq failure, one reached on the initial state and one on the second, and
# they read 75 and 76. The page's last section rests on that pair, so neither
# row may be relaxed to the other's code.
#
# Exit codes TLC uses here:
#   0    all checks passed
#   12   an invariant was violated by a state
#   75   evaluation failed while TLC was working on the initial state, with no
#        behavior printed
#   76   evaluation of an invariant failed on a state reached by a step, with
#        the behavior printed
#   150  parse or semantic error in the module

Conveyor.tla|Conveyor.cfg|0|4|a sequence is a function on 1..Len(s), EXCEPT included
Conveyor.tla|ConveyorZero.cfg|76||index 0 is outside the domain, so the run stops
Conveyor.tla|ConveyorSlice.cfg|76||a past-the-end slice reached on the second state
Spool.tla|SpoolType.cfg|0|7|wire \in Seq(Colors) is a test, so the invariant holds
Spool.tla|SpoolBounded.cfg|0|7|and the finite bounded union holds over the same states
Spool.tla|SpoolEnumerated.cfg|75||quantifying over Seq(Colors) is refused outright
Spool.tla|SpoolAny.cfg|75|0|and drawing Init from it leaves nothing to check
Pallet.tla|Pallet.cfg|0|3|Append adds one element, \o joins two sequences flat
Pallet.tla|PalletSameLength.cfg|12||so the same layers sit at two different lengths
Crate.tla|Crate.cfg|0|2|Head and Tail behind a guard that rules out the empty crate
Crate.tla|CrateBareHead.cfg|76||Head of the empty sequence stops the run
Crate.tla|CrateBareTail.cfg|76||and Tail of it stops the run the same way
